# Microsoft's Windows.Devices.Midi2 package, fetched from nuget.org into wms/.
# See the header of build.bat for exactly which three files go here and where
# they come from inside the package.
#
# It is MIT and we ARE allowed to redistribute it - but MIT requires the
# copyright notice to travel with it, and that notice is not in LICENSE yet
# (Task 7 Step 1 of the plan puts it there, and calls it a legal obligation
# rather than documentation). Until then nothing of Microsoft's is committed
# here. This is the same arrangement native/ASIOSDK/ already uses, and
# build.bat prints the fetch instructions when the folder is empty.
wms/

# The C++/WinRT projection. Thousands of generated headers derived from
# wms/Windows.Devices.Midi2.winmd plus the Windows SDK; build.bat regenerates
# it on every run, so a checked-in copy could only ever be a stale one.
winrt/

# Build artefacts. *.dll, *.lib, *.exe, *.obj and *.pdb are already excluded
# repository-wide; these are the ones this folder produces on top of those.
*.exp
Windows.Devices.Midi2.pri

# runs/ holds the binaries staged for the controller to run one per reboot,
# including the two INJECTED builds. Injected builds must never reach the
# repository - a defect deliberately compiled in is the one artefact that must
# not outlive the measurement it was made for. selftest-COMMANDS.txt says what
# is in there and how each one was produced.
runs/
